---
import FeaturesLayout from '../../layouts/FeaturesLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<FeaturesLayout
  currentSlug="tab-configuration"
  title="Tab Configuration - Reorder & hide compodocx entity tabs"
  description="compodocx entity tabs - Info, API, Source, DOM Tree, Theming, Playground. Reorder, relabel, or hide them with navTabConfig and compose their sections."
>
  <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary text-lg">
    Each entity page renders one or more tabs: <em>Info</em>, <em>API</em>, <em>Source</em>, plus
    <em>README</em>, <em>Template</em>, <em>Styles</em>, <em>Theming</em>, <em>DOM Tree</em>,
    <em>Examples</em>, and <em>Playground</em> when there is data for them. Tab visibility is data-driven.
    Sections only render when there&rsquo;s something to show.
  </p>

  <h2>Auto-visibility</h2>
  <ul class="text-cdx-text-secondary mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm">
    <li>
      <strong class="text-cdx-text">Theming</strong> appears on component pages when the component&rsquo;s
      styles hold documented tokens or mixins, and on component and directive pages when a file listed
      in
      <code class="cdx-code">styleFiles</code> names them with <code class="cdx-code">@themes</code
      >.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-cdx-text">Examples</strong> appears when at least one
      <code class="cdx-code">&lt;example-url&gt;</code> marker is present in the class JSDoc.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-cdx-text">Info</strong>, <strong class="text-cdx-text">API</strong>,
      <strong class="text-cdx-text">Source</strong> are always present where applicable.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reorder, relabel, or hide tabs</h2>
  <p>
    <code class="cdx-code">navTabConfig</code> takes a list of <code class="cdx-code"
      >{'{ id, label }'}</code
    >
    objects. Tabs you don&rsquo;t list are hidden. IDs: <code class="cdx-code">info</code>,
    <code class="cdx-code">readme</code>, <code class="cdx-code">api</code>,
    <code class="cdx-code">source</code>, <code class="cdx-code">templateData</code>,
    <code class="cdx-code">styleData</code>, <code class="cdx-code">theming</code>,
    <code class="cdx-code">tree</code>, <code class="cdx-code">example</code>, and
    <code class="cdx-code">playground</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Section composition</h2>
  <p>
    Within each tab, sections render in a default order. Sections without data are skipped: a
    component without inputs simply omits the inputs row, no empty heading. The config-only keys
    <code class="cdx-code">infoTabSections</code>, <code class="cdx-code">apiTabSections</code>, and
    <code class="cdx-code">themingTabSections</code> replace that list in full, so name every section
    you want. The IDs are in the <a
      href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}guides/options/#tab-sections`}
      class="text-cdx-primary underline-offset-2 hover:underline">options guide</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>Theming tab sections</h2>
  <p>
    The Theming tab&rsquo;s composition is configurable per project via the JSON config file (no CLI
    flag). Pass a subset of <code class="cdx-code"
      >['overview', 'index', 'tokens', 'mixins', 'source']</code
    >
    in the order you want them to appear:
  </p>

  <CodeBlock
    lang="json"
    code={`{
  "themingTabSections": ["overview", "tokens"]
}`}
  />

  <p>
    The example above hides the per-tab token index, the mixins, and the source preview. Tab
    visibility itself is not affected. The Theming tab still shows whenever theming data exists.
  </p>

  <h2>Deeper customization</h2>
  <p>
    For changes beyond reordering or hiding sections (custom rendering, additional members,
    project-specific layouts) use the JS-based template override system via
    <code class="cdx-code">--templates &lt;path&gt;</code>. Each overridable surface (page-level and
    block-level) is a JS partial exporting
    <code class="cdx-code">function(data, helpers) {'...'}</code>. Coming from Handlebars overrides?
    Rewrite them by hand with the cookbook in the migration guide. Handlebars files are skipped with
    one warning.
  </p>
</FeaturesLayout>
